A||||5||85ZainoGT||need some help with the car I just bought||||1||
Z||000000||85ZainoGT||11-11-2001||10:06 PM||||well... I just need to know how to do a few things and I need to know a few things..<P> 1. My brakes are squeaking, how do I fix/check that deal?<BR> 2. the 2 vents in the corners of the trunk lid.. one side doesnt have any screws holding it down.. can I just go buy screws anywhere? what size?<BR> 3. my car as rear defrost, I should be able to tint my back window still right?  someone told me its not good too...<BR> 4. when I turn the wheel almost all the way either way, I hear a sound, maybe rubbing? is this possible? common?<BR> 5. could I just take my 2.8 out and slap a 3.4 in there for less than 1000 dollar bills? because the 2.8 has 136k on it.. <P>  I think that is it for now... thanks  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Paul Ventimiglia<BR>1987 Gold GT 2.8L<BR>All the options :)<BR>  pics are coming :)||||reg||1
Z||000001||85ZainoGT||11-11-2001||10:07 PM||||oh geez, jus realized this isnt tech, im putting it there too, help if you can thanks! sorry!||||reg||1
Z||000002||Old Lar||11-11-2001||10:59 PM||||1. Check for brake pad wear thickness. Replace brake pads resurface rotors, if there is enough other wise replace rotors too.<BR>2. Junk yard scavenger hunt for screws, or call Fiero recyle places for screws.<BR>3. Why bother, most home grown tint jobs look like he!!.  The defrost wires may not give an all over flat surface for the tint film to stick nicely to the glass.<BR>4. Rubbing Possible yes, common, No.. Check step 1. Check tire size, too big?<BR>5.  Yes.  You could slap a 3.4L in for $1000, then you'd have a 3.4 with 136k in your Fiero when your done.  It would cost you twice that if you want it done right with a good engine, and 4 times that for a new crate engine.||||reg||1
Z||000003||SKIDMARK||11-11-2001||11:15 PM||||I agree with LAR. The brakes may just need cleaned or some anti-squeel on the BACK of the pads. Mine are new with new rotors and everything and they still squeel a little. If they squeel all the time they you probably need new pads and maybe rotors. <BR>The tint will work but you have to get the right person to do it. Will cost more than it's worth. The 3.4 swap can be done for $1000 or so IF you do it yourself with no frills and re-use all the 2.8 intake, oilpan, valve covers, water pump, timing case cover, and if you can get a decent 3.4 for about $600. I would suggest at least a new oil pump, water pump, and timing chain. You also will need a new flex plate and all the top end and timing cover gaskets. A lot of work for a used motor with no guarantee.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Doni Hagan||11-11-2001||11:18 PM||||DON'T TRY TO DO THE REAR TINT YOURSELF if you have the defroster. It's worth the money paid to have it done by someone you can annoy if it's not done right.||||reg||1
Z||000005||BOILERMAKER||11-12-2001||07:11 AM||||I haven't had much time on here, but had a moment and thought I would chime in.<P>The rubbing you are hearing is the inner fender rubbing on the left front tire because it lost a screw holding it on and then droops down to hit the tire.  No big deal and I may have an extra we can put on it (I just have to get out of work long enough ... don't think I have forgotten about you).<P>I've had to take window tint off of a car with rear defrost and it was a huge PITA.  I wouldn't recommend going this route, but hey, it's your car, do what you want and not what everyone else wants.<P>Hey, I got the 3800 to fire up last night!!!!!!||||reg||1
